  "prompt": "Below is a text based on a real interview with a real public figure. It may have been disguised: names of people, places, nations, organizations and events may have been replaced, the setting may have been moved to a different era or geography, and the wording may have been paraphrased. The speaker's positions were kept.\n\nDo not search the web. Answer only from your own knowledge.\n\n1. Which real-world conflict, country and period do you think the original text is about? Give up to 3 distinct alternative source contexts.\n2. Who do you think the real speaker is? Give up to 5 distinct candidates.\n\nConfidence values are probabilities from 0 to 100. Within each list separately, their sum must not exceed 100. Any remaining probability represents other or unknown possibilities; do not redistribute it among the listed guesses. Give fewer guesses, or an empty list, when the evidence is insufficient. Do not list overlapping descriptions of the same source context as separate guesses.\n\nReply with JSON only, no other text, in exactly this shape:\n\n{\n  \"context\": [\n    {\"guess\": \"...\", \"confidence\": 0}\n  ],\n  \"speakers\": [\n    {\"name\": \"...\", \"confidence\": 0, \"clues_for\": \"...\", \"clues_against\": \"...\"}\n  ],\n  \"most_revealing_clue\": \"...\"\n}\n\nTEXT:\n---\n{{TEXT}}\n---\n"
